# Handwritten Digit Recognition using Neural Networks (MNIST)

An end-to-end deep learning project that trains a **Multilayer Perceptron (MLP)**
to classify handwritten digits (0–9) from the MNIST dataset.

## 🚀 Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Clone / create the project
mkdir mnist-digit-recognition && cd mnist-digit-recognition

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate          # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Run the complete pipeline (train + evaluate)
python main.py
```

## Predict from an image

After training the model, launch the image uploader:

```bash
python -m src.upload_app
```

Choose an image containing one handwritten digit. The app accepts PNG, JPG,
BMP, GIF, and TIFF images, then displays the predicted digit and confidence.
For best results, use a clear image with one digit and minimal surrounding text.